  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-5.0$ | $-4.0$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.0$ | $0.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation.\n\n${g}^{\u2032}(-1)\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(-1) & \u2248\\frac{g(-1+1)-g(-1-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0)-g(-2)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.0-(-4.0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
